# Description
# This module is used to passively / non-destructively measure the energy 
# of the stored electron beam through its connection with electron spin 
# precession, beam polarisation, Touschek scattering and beam loss.
# Check the associated confluence for a complete physics explanation.
# 
# This diagnostic kicks the spin vectors off-axis using the bunch-by-bunch 
# and measures the corresponding increase in beam loss when the kicker 
# frequency is resonant with the spin tune. This resonant frequency encodes the 
# beam energy.
#
# Diagnostic workflow:
# - Initialisation (connect to PVs, logging config, etc.)
# - Collect baseline data (beam loss with no kicker)
# - BbB kicker -> ON
# - EXPERIMENT LOOP
# -- Consists of sweeping the kicker frequency over a given range
# -- Calling _log_data() at 10 Hz
# -- report progress at 1 Hz
# -- Watching for abort requests, injections, beam dumps, wiggler ramps
# -- END
# - Cleanup (turn off kicker, reset BLM settings, etc.)
# - Data analysis pipeline
# - Report results (to GUI)
#
# The ResonantDepolarisation() class can be removed from memory and spun 
# up again, but this would mean connecting to PVs every time. The class can 
# easily sit idle and wait for a subsequent call to start_experiment(). 
# The PV connections are cached.
# 
# From template parameters
# DEVICE - Normal resdep PV prefix: e.g. SR00RDP01
